<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>World news and headlines - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 14:33:41 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>The 'other kick-off': NGOs warn of domestic violence spike during World Cup</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-the-other-kick-off-ngos-warn-of-domestic-violence-spike-during-world-cup</link><description>
With the World Cup in full swing, several NGOs have launched awareness campaigns to prevent domestic abuse – incidents of which studies have shown increase on match nights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8063559a-7474-11f1-a23a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8JT2L6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8063559a-7474-11f1-a23a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8JT2L6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6cdae03c-752e-11f1-bff2-cfc0d8bf5aea</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 14:25:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8063559a-7474-11f1-a23a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8JT2L6.jpg">AFP - SCOTT HEPPELL</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Pope Leo urges US and Europe to do more for migrants on 4th July anniversary</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-pope-leo-urges-us-and-europe-to-do-more-for-migrants-on-4th-july-anniversary</link><description>
Pope Leo has urged his fellow Americans to welcome and protect immigrants as the United States marked the 250th anniversary of its independence on Saturday. During a visit to the Italian island of Lampedusa he also pressed Europe to do more for people fleeing war and poverty.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5a62981c-778d-11f1-a02c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9932WN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5a62981c-778d-11f1-a02c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9932WN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">59600404-77a1-11f1-80a4-05107bf6196b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 12:10:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5a62981c-778d-11f1-a02c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9932WN.jpg">AFP - TIZIANA FABI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>United States at 250: Looking beyond the founding fathers to unsung revolutionaries</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-united-states-at-250-looks-beyond-founding-fathers-to-hidden-revolutionaries</link><description>
The American Revolution is often examined through the lives of towering figures such as George Washington and Benjamin Franklin. But as the United States marks 250 years since the Declaration of Independence, RFI uncovers the stories of an enslaved spy, a woman who fought disguised as a man and an Oneida healer, all of whom helped shape the fight. Their stories begin long before 1776, with European colonisation, the dispossession of indigenous people and the labour of enslaved Africans.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28e59b5c-7159-11f1-8e9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/nancy-hart.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28e59b5c-7159-11f1-8e9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/nancy-hart.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">939f62d2-7494-11f1-a1c6-d71d79a3479e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 08:50:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28e59b5c-7159-11f1-8e9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/nancy-hart.jpg">© Domaine public</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US turns 250 as Trump warns of 'attack' on American identity</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260704-us-turns-250-as-trump-warns-of-attack-on-american-identity</link><description>
America turns 250 on Saturday – a landmark birthday that coincides with a time of deep national division and a president determined to seize the festive centre stage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0af7efa2-776f-11f1-8423-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d89394b4bc7eb55ed314f11865b9a00b75f2939d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0af7efa2-776f-11f1-8423-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d89394b4bc7eb55ed314f11865b9a00b75f2939d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c187212-776f-11f1-80c8-f59519eefc02</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 06:10:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0af7efa2-776f-11f1-8423-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d89394b4bc7eb55ed314f11865b9a00b75f2939d.jpg">© Mandel NGAN / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Why Israel's recognition of the Armenian genocide is raising new questions</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260703-why-israel-s-recognition-of-the-armenian-genocide-is-raising-new-questions</link><description>
Israel's recognition of the 1915 Armenian genocide has ended decades of caution over one of the world's most politically sensitive historical events. The cabinet decision, announced last week and still awaiting parliamentary ratification, has also prompted questions over whether it is driven more by current regional politics than by historical recognition.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1d4d398e-211a-11f0-b3c2-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25113649420300.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1d4d398e-211a-11f0-b3c2-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25113649420300.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e9a85370-746f-11f1-b2bf-5775698aa900</guid><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 16:01:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1d4d398e-211a-11f0-b3c2-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25113649420300.jpg">AP - Hayk Baghdasaryan</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Hunt for Ukrainian woman after Monaco bomb attack targeting sanctioned tycoon</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260703-hunt-for-ukrainian-woman-after-monaco-bomb-attack-targeting-sanctioned-tycoon</link><description>
Interpol have issued a worldwide alert over a Ukrainian woman suspected of planting a bomb in Monaco that injured three people, including a tycoon of Ukrainian origin. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c6cff016-7527-11f1-ad90-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26181322542006.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c6cff016-7527-11f1-ad90-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26181322542006.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a9817ce-76bc-11f1-a05f-a3670709bd60</guid><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 11:07:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c6cff016-7527-11f1-ad90-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26181322542006.jpg">© Philippe Magoni / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Google loses final appeal against EU’s record €4.1bn anti-trust fine</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260702-google-loses-final-appeal-against-eu-s-record-%E2%82%AC4-1bn-anti-trust-fine</link><description>
The European Union’s top court has dismissed Google’s final appeal against a record €4.1 billion anti-trust fine, confirming one of Brussels’ most significant victories in its long-running effort to rein in Big Tech.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e56bb90-75ef-11f1-acfb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B67G7G6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e56bb90-75ef-11f1-acfb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B67G7G6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a78c30fc-75ea-11f1-ad04-cfc389d0d340</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 09:48:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e56bb90-75ef-11f1-acfb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B67G7G6.jpg">AFP - KIRILL KUDRYAVTSEV</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Thousands rush to get tickets for Bayeux Tapestry's UK show</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260701-thousands-rush-to-get-tickets-for-bayeux-tapestry-s-uk-show</link><description>
Thousands rushed to get tickets Wednesday for the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition in London, with the 11th-century artwork depicting the 1066 Norman conquest of England set to be transported from France for its first showing in the UK.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09a31122-5faa-11f1-8f11-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4854842b2950ba8ef1c9b01c8b5129e96b7395e2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09a31122-5faa-11f1-8f11-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4854842b2950ba8ef1c9b01c8b5129e96b7395e2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ed4f882-7535-11f1-bedb-c774f26789d8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 10:14:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09a31122-5faa-11f1-8f11-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4854842b2950ba8ef1c9b01c8b5129e96b7395e2.jpg">© Lou BENOIST / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU rolls out small parcel levy to stem flow of cheap goods</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260701-eu-rolls-out-small-parcel-levy-to-stem-flow-of-cheap-goods</link><description>
The European Union will impose a three-euro duty on cheap parcels entering the 27-nation bloc from Wednesday, in a bid to stem a surge in low-value packages, mainly from China.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8de39136-15af-11f1-a2de-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/1820039-des-douaniers-controlent-des-colis-dans-un-centre-de-tri-en-decembre-2022.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8de39136-15af-11f1-a2de-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/1820039-des-douaniers-controlent-des-colis-dans-un-centre-de-tri-en-decembre-2022.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0de7d82c-7485-11f1-8717-432561169cd3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 06:54:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8de39136-15af-11f1-a2de-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/1820039-des-douaniers-controlent-des-colis-dans-un-centre-de-tri-en-decembre-2022.jpg">© Romain Longieras / Hans Lucas via AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ireland takes over EU presidency with French naval help on security</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260701-ireland-takes-over-eu-presidency-with-french-naval-help-on-security</link><description>
Ireland takes over the rotating presidency of the Council of the European Union on Wednesday with French and British military assets expected to help protect a six-month programme of high-level meetings, as Dublin prepares for what security officials describe as an unusually demanding operation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/36cabbfe-7478-11f1-bfb3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33GL4GB.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/36cabbfe-7478-11f1-bfb3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33GL4GB.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21297916-745f-11f1-83a2-c9a0ace6ef83</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 06:09:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/36cabbfe-7478-11f1-bfb3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33GL4GB.jpg">AFP - RICHARD A. BROOKS</source><dc:creator>David Coffey</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Mbappe scores twice as France breeze past Sweden into World Cup last 16</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260630-mbappe-scores-twice-as-france-breeze-past-sweden-into-world-cup-last-16</link><description>
Kylian Mbappe scored twice and Michael Olise was in scintillating form as France beat Sweden 3-0 at the World Cup on Tuesday and set up a last-16 clash with Paraguay.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4add8ada-74d8-11f1-8c41-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/900bc06b40f25528e7c764cb704d7f2a113ece0e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4add8ada-74d8-11f1-8c41-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/900bc06b40f25528e7c764cb704d7f2a113ece0e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4bc80434-74d8-11f1-bf75-fda9116ca60d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 23:06:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4add8ada-74d8-11f1-8c41-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/900bc06b40f25528e7c764cb704d7f2a113ece0e.jpg">© Jewel SAMAD / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Israel formally recognises Armenian genocide in rebuke to Turkey</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260629-israel-formally-recognises-armenian-genocide-in-rebuke-to-turkey</link><description>
The Israeli government on Sunday unanimously recognised the massacres of Armenians during World War I as genocide, a move widely seen as a rebuke to Turkey and a stark signal of the deepening rift between the two countries. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/841d145c-588c-11ee-b683-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/armenia%20genocide%20monument%201.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/841d145c-588c-11ee-b683-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/armenia%20genocide%20monument%201.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ecb1caa-73b9-11f1-b318-c36db13bf4d8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 13:58:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/841d145c-588c-11ee-b683-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/armenia%20genocide%20monument%201.jpg">© RFI/Jan van der Made</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>French journalist Gleizes marks one year in Algerian prison as RSF renews appeal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260629-french-journalist-gleizes-marks-one-year-in-algerian-prison-as-rsf-renews-appeal</link><description>
French sports journalist Christophe Gleizes has now spent a year in detention in Algeria, prompting fresh calls from Reporters Without Borders and his family for his immediate release and a presidential pardon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a03f9dce-73a2-11f1-9966-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4QX2YL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a03f9dce-73a2-11f1-9966-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4QX2YL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">683b8986-7390-11f1-aa37-7d8eb55a1ec6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 13:26:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a03f9dce-73a2-11f1-9966-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4QX2YL.jpg">AFP - MIGUEL MEDINA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>European heatwave continues to top records amid high alerts in the east</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260627-european-heatwave-continues-to-top-records-amid-high-alerts-in-the-east</link><description>
Tens of millions face a weekend of extreme temperatures in Europe as a deadly heatwave moves eastwards, with German forecasters warning that more records could be broken and eastern countries issuing a slew of red alerts for the coming days.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/90fa4050-713e-11f1-9bde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-25T151834Z-985103065-RC231MAW2D7O-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HEAT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/90fa4050-713e-11f1-9bde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-25T151834Z-985103065-RC231MAW2D7O-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HEAT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">beea3ec0-7242-11f1-9935-6f8bbe7fb1bc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 16:10:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/90fa4050-713e-11f1-9bde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-25T151834Z-985103065-RC231MAW2D7O-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HEAT.jpg">REUTERS - Gonzalo Fuentes</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>UK to introduce new legal routes for asylum seekers, refugees</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260627-uk-to-introduce-new-legal-routes-for-asylum-seekers-refugees</link><description>
The UK interior ministry has announced it will create new legal routes for asylum seekers, including allowing community organisations to sponsor refugees based on a similar system in Canada.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/433abba8-817d-11f0-8ae7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25234663094358.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/433abba8-817d-11f0-8ae7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25234663094358.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b92f4e2-7230-11f1-a3c9-851ac519f066</guid><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 14:16:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/433abba8-817d-11f0-8ae7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25234663094358.jpg">© Alberto Pezzali / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Turkey opposition worries that Europe is sacrificing democracy for security</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/special-features/20260627-turkey-opposition-chp-says-europe-is-sacrificing-democracy-for-security</link><description>
Turkey's main opposition says its Western allies are failing to respond as a widening crackdown by President Recep Tayyip Erdogan's government targets its leaders and elected mayors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dcc5897e-580a-11f1-a3a3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-24T165816Z-925380860-RC2SFLALVD22-RTRMADP-3-TURKEY-OPPOSITION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dcc5897e-580a-11f1-a3a3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-24T165816Z-925380860-RC2SFLALVD22-RTRMADP-3-TURKEY-OPPOSITION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6451578-7175-11f1-9724-9b37fc2e51ce</guid><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 09:03:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Lebanon, Israel and US sign trilateral framework pact</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260626-lebanon-israel-and-us-sign-trilateral-framework-pact</link><description>
Lebanon, Israel and the United States on Friday signed a trilateral framework agreement aimed at paving the way for a peace deal between the two long-time Middle East adversaries.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1c9577be-718b-11f1-9e57-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cd28488ede66119c11a363905d9da6756f451321.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1c9577be-718b-11f1-9e57-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cd28488ede66119c11a363905d9da6756f451321.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d66f87a-718b-11f1-8429-33b33717f8fa</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 18:16:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1c9577be-718b-11f1-9e57-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/cd28488ede66119c11a363905d9da6756f451321.jpg">© SAUL LOEB / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Israel's targeting of Gaza's children proves genocidal intent, UN inquiry finds</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260626-israel-s-targeting-of-gaza-children-proves-genocidal-intent-un-inquiry-says</link><description>
The deliberate targeting of Palestinian children is central to a United Nations-mandated report's conclusion that Israel is committing genocide in Gaza. The commission argues that children have not only been victims of the war, but have been targeted in ways that help establish genocidal intent. Israel has dismissed the findings of the report, released this week, as "defamatory".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0862b8a8-493a-11f0-a15b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25140303784353.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0862b8a8-493a-11f0-a15b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25140303784353.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0356a1c0-714e-11f1-9c0f-bf9829427aa8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 15:01:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0862b8a8-493a-11f0-a15b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25140303784353.jpg">© Abdel Kareem Hana / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Brexit at 10: What price has the UK paid for 'taking back control'?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260626-brexit-at-10-what-price-has-the-uk-paid-for-taking-back-control</link><description>
Ten years after the United Kingdom voted to leave the European Union, Brexit supporters still see this as a historic act of sovereignty, while critics point to the resulting economic damage and political division. 
